# Apex Day — Connect IQ build configuration (Connect IQ SDK >= 6 grammar).
#
# SDK 6+ derives source/, resources/ and the launcher icon from the manifest
# location (this folder), so the jungle only pins the manifest and enables
# strict typechecking. Legacy keys (project.sourcePath / project.resources /
# project.type / project.baseIcon) are REJECTED by the current jungle parser.
#
# NOTE: no project.typecheck override — the official SDK samples compile at
# the default (gradual) level; strict adds a cross-build-scope diagnostic that
# false-positives on the canonical AppBase entry-method pattern used by
# Garmin's own BackgroundTimer sample (verified against SDK 9.2.0).
#
# Build one command per device (key first: java -jar <SDK>/bin/monkeybrains.jar -a -o devkey.pem
# or `openssl genrsa -traditional -out devkey.pem 2048`):
#   monkeyc -f monkey.jungle -y devkey.pem -w -o bin/ApexDay-fenix7pro.prg -d fenix7pro
# Unit tests (simulator):
#   monkeyc -f monkey.jungle -y devkey.pem -w -o bin/ApexDay-test.prg -d fenix7pro --unit-test
#   monkeydo bin/ApexDay-test.prg fenix7pro -t
project.manifest = manifest.xml
